// Screen capture (wayle's screenshot, region freeze, color picker, and
// screencast producer): wlr-screencopy copies a whole output or a
// region; the ext-image-copy-capture session model (with the
// ext-image-capture-source output and foreign-toplevel sources and the
// ext-foreign-toplevel-list enumeration) is the compositor-neutral
// successor that also captures single windows; linux-dmabuf imports a
// GPU buffer as a wl_buffer for the zero-copy screencopy target; and
// Hyprland's toplevel-export captures a window by its address. The ext,
// linux, and hyprland names do not start with wlr_, so the package
// clause is renamed like the protocols above. The dmabuf binding's
// params.created event builds a wl_buffer through wl's unexported
// initializer; the capture package only uses create_immed, so that
// event's buffer is registered without its release-handler map.
//go:generate sh -c "go run github.com/neurlang/wayland/cmd/wayland-scanner -i wlr-screencopy-unstable-v1.xml && sed -i '1i // Code generated by github.com/neurlang/wayland/cmd/wayland-scanner. DO NOT EDIT.' wlr-screencopy-unstable-v1.xml.go && gofmt -w wlr-screencopy-unstable-v1.xml.go"
